{meta: title Too Much Mountain Dew}
{meta: x_lyrics_source bluegrass-lyrics}
{meta: x_lyrics_url https://www.bluegrasslyrics.com/song/too-much-mountain-dew/}

{start_of_verse}
Too much Mountain dew
Too much Mountain dew
Dewey left a-drinking
Too much Mountain dew
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Now Dewey left this morning
Feeling oh so fine
With a jug in one hand
Drinking on his mind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Now the hottest sun was shining
While Dewey laid in the shade
Drinking from a bottle
Home brew that he made
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Now drinking was a weakness
That he couldn’t hide
Had one drink too many
Poor old Dewey died
{end_of_verse}

